<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Soufrière (Saint Vincent)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Soufrière is an active volcano forming the northern part of Saint Vincent in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, the island's highest peak at about 1,234 metres. Its eruption of May 1902, a day before that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-pelee">Mount Pelée</a> on Martinique, killed about 1,600 people, many of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a> and estate workers. Later eruptions in 1979 and 2021 forced large evacuations but caused few deaths.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-soufriere-saint-vincent.jpg" alt="La Soufrière (Saint Vincent)" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soufriere.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
